@startuml
title Online read and writeback
actor Teacher as T
participant "Local server" as S
participant "Teacher browser" as B
participant Google as G
T -> S : authorize on localhost
S --> B : redirect with single-use state
B -> G : sign in and consent
G --> B : redirect to registered loopback callback
B -> S : authorization code + state
S -> S : validate teacher session + state
S -> G : exchange code (web application client)
G --> S : tokens
S -> S : tokens in memory only
S --> B : redirect to clean teacher URL
B -> S : GET authorization status
S --> B : authorized / safe error (no tokens)
T -> S : spreadsheet URL or ID
S -> G : read cell values, merges, sheet metadata
G --> S : source grid
S -> S : infer single / grouped items and targets
S --> T : mapping preview / ambiguity errors
T -> S : confirm mapping / start / end
T -> S : write winners
S -> G : reread target structure + baseline
alt conflict or missing write permission
 S --> T : conflict / forbidden; skip affected question
else unchanged
 S -> G : batchUpdate UpdateCells stringValue / winning targets only
 alt confirmed response and matching readback
  S --> T : verified target statuses
 else timeout or ambiguous response
  S --> T : pending verification
  T -> S : verify or retry
  S -> G : read target values before any retry
  alt all expected strings and mapping unchanged
   S --> T : verified (content matches)
  else all baseline values and mapping unchanged
   S -> G : one atomic retry for the whole question
   S -> G : read back strings and structure
   S --> T : verified / conflict / pending
  else mixed values or changed mapping
   S --> T : conflict / no retry
  end
 end
end
note over T,G
Teacher pauses external editing during writeback.
Google Sheets API has no cell compare-and-swap.
No secret values appear in messages or logs.
end note
@enduml
